    "title": "One dead after a pickup truck towing a pickup truck fishtails out of control - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dailyn Wells ,\n8 hours ago\nDALLAM COUNTY, Texas (KAMR/KCIT) — The Texas Department of Public Safety reports that a wreck on US Highway 54 involving three vehicles resulted in multiple injuries and one death.\nAccording to DPS, the wreck occurred around 9:30 a.m. on Oct. 6, 2026, on US Highway 54 about 2 miles Northwest of FM 3212.\nWater safety notice in effect for Lake Meredith Preliminary investigation revealed that a 2011 Chevrolet pickup was towing a 2006 Chevrolet pickup traveling southwest on US 54 when a 2015 Ford pickup, towing a trailer, driven by Robert Spielman, 70, of Dalhart, was heading northeast on US 54.\nDPS said the 2011 Chevrolet pickup tried to avoid hitting the back of a truck-tractor semi-trailer ahead of it. The 2006 Chevrolet pickup that was being towed began fishtailing. This caused both the 2011 Chevrolet pickup and 2006 Chevrolet pickup to enter the northeast lanes of US 54, resulting in the 2015 Ford pickup colliding with the 2011 Chevrolet pickup.\nSpielman, the driver of the 2015 Ford pickup, was transported to a nearby hospital, where he was later pronounced dead as a result of the injuries sustained in the wreck. The driver of the pickup was towing another pickup and was transported to Coon Memorial Hospital-Dalhart for minor injuries. The passenger of the truck being towed was transported with serious injuries.\nFor the latest Amarillo news and regional updates, check with MyHighPlains.com and tune in to KAMR Local 4 News at 5:00, 6:00, and 10:00 p.m. and Fox 14 News at 9:00 p.m. CST.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KAMR - MyHighPlains.com.\n1",
    "summary": "According to DPS, the wreck occurred around 9:30 a.m. on Oct. 6, 2026, on US Highway 54 about 2 miles Northwest of FM 3212. Water safety notice in effect for Lake Meredith Preliminary investigation revealed that a 2011 Chevrolet pickup was towing a 2006 Chevrolet pickup traveling southwest on US 54 when a 2015 Ford pickup, towing a trailer, driven by Robert Spielman, 70, of Dalhart, was heading northeast on US 54. DPS said the 2011 Chevrolet pickup tried to avoid hitting the back of a truck-tractor semi-trailer ahead of it.",
